meta {
  name: Get a book
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/books/{{bookId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq ready
}

tests {
  test("ingest finished", function () {
    const book = res.getBody();
    expect(book.status, book.error || "no error reported").to.equal("ready");
    expect(book.owner_is_me).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  Poll this for ingest status: `uploaded -> parsing -> chunking -> embedding -> ready`.

  A `failed` book carries a sentence in `error` that is fit to show its owner, not a
  stack trace — and `Retry ingest` puts it back on the queue.

  `owner_is_me` is computed server-side from the caller. The owner's id is deliberately
  not in the payload: the UI needs one bit to decide whether to offer Share and Delete,
  and shipping the raw id would hand every reader of the shared library a list of user
  ids to answer a yes/no question with.
}
